{
  "id": "nn_msy4smdb_mj9sf5r4u",
  "title": "Array hard ",
  "content": "<h1>3 SUM — COMPLETE NOTES</h1><h2>Approach 1: BRUTE FORCE</h2><blockquote><p><strong>Problem:</strong> Given an array of integers, find <strong>all unique triplets</strong> whose sum is <code>0</code>.</p></blockquote><hr><h1>1. Problem Statement</h1><p>You are given an array of integers.</p><p>Your task is to find <strong>all the triplets</strong> such that:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr[i] + arr[j] + arr[k] = 0</code></pre></div><h3>Important Conditions</h3><p>There are <strong>three critical points</strong>:</p><h3>① A triplet contains exactly 3 elements</h3><p>For example:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>because:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 2 + (-1) = 0</code></pre></div><hr><h3>② Same array element/index cannot be taken more than once</h3><p>This means:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i ≠ j\nj ≠ k\ni ≠ k</code></pre></div><p>For example, if the array contains:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>we can take:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1(index 0) + 2(index 1) + -1(index 2)</code></pre></div><p>because these are <strong>three different positions</strong>.</p><p>But if there is only one <code>2</code>:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>we cannot do:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">2 + 2 + (-4)</code></pre></div><p>just because the sum is <code>0</code>.</p><p>Why?</p><p>Because there is only <strong>one <code>2</code></strong> available.</p><hr><h1>2. Duplicate Triplets Are NOT Allowed</h1><p>This is extremely important.</p><p>Suppose:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>We can generate:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>But we can also encounter the same values in another order:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>or:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[2, -1, -1]</code></pre></div><p>All three represent the <strong>same triplet</strong>.</p><p>Because:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + (-1) + 2 = 0</code></pre></div><p>So the answer should contain only:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>and NOT:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]\n[-1, -1, 2]\n[2, -1, -1]</code></pre></div><h3>Therefore:</h3><blockquote><p><strong>We only need unique triplets.</strong></p></blockquote><p>The order of the triplets in the final answer can be anything.</p><hr><h1>3. Example</h1><p>Suppose:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr = [-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>Some possible triplets are:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 0 + 1 = 0\n-1 + 2 + (-1) = 0</code></pre></div><p>So the answer is:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[\n    [-1, 0, 1],\n    [-1, -1, 2]\n]</code></pre></div><p>Notice:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 0, 1]</code></pre></div><p>and</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[0, -1, 1]</code></pre></div><p>would be duplicates.</p><p>We only keep one.</p><hr><h1>4. First Thought → Brute Force</h1><p>When the interviewer asks this question, the <strong>first solution</strong> that should come to your mind is:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Why not try out all the triplets?</strong></p></blockquote><p>A triplet has:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">1st element\n2nd element\n3rd element</code></pre></div><p>So we need to try every possible combination of:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i\nj\nk</code></pre></div><p>Then simply check:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr[i] + arr[j] + arr[k] == 0</code></pre></div><p>If yes:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">→ this is one of our triplets</code></pre></div><hr><h1>5. How Do We Generate ALL Triplets?</h1><p>Suppose:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr = [-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>We need three positions:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i → first\nj → second\nk → third</code></pre></div><p>Visualize it like this:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">        i       j       k\n        ↓       ↓       ↓\n       [-1,  0,  1,  2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><hr><h2>Step 1: Fix <code>i</code></h2><p>Suppose:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i = 0</code></pre></div><p>Then:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">        i\n        ↓\n       [-1,  0,  1,  2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>Now what can be our second element?</p><p>It can be any element <strong>after <code>i</code></strong>:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">          j\n          ↓\n       [-1,  0,  1,  2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>or:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">       [-1,  0,  1,  2, -1, -4]\n              ↑\n              j</code></pre></div><p>or:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">       [-1,  0,  1,  2, -1, -4]\n                   ↑\n                   j</code></pre></div><p>and so on.</p><h3>Therefore:</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">j = i + 1 → n - 1</code></pre></div><p>There is no point in going backward because that would repeat combinations.</p><hr><h1>6. Now We Need the Third Element</h1><p>Once <code>i</code> and <code>j</code> are fixed:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i → first element\nj → second element</code></pre></div><p>The third element <code>k</code> can again be any element <strong>after <code>j</code></strong>.</p><p>Visual:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">       i       j       k\n       ↓       ↓       ↓\n      [-1,  0,  1,  2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>Therefore:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">k = j + 1 → n - 1</code></pre></div><hr><h1>7. The Three Loops</h1><p>So the complete brute-force structure becomes:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">for i\n    for j\n        for k</code></pre></div><p>More specifically:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; n; i++)\n{\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> j = i + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>; j &lt; n; j++)\n    {\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> k = j + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>; k &lt; n; k++)\n        {\n            <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// check triplet</span>\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></div><h3>Why these starting points?</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i → 0\nj → i + 1\nk → j + 1</code></pre></div><p>Because we always want:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i &lt; j &lt; k</code></pre></div><p>Visual:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">INDEX:\n\n  0   1   2   3   4   5\n  ↓   ↓   ↓\n  i   j   k\n\nAlways:\n\ni &lt; j &lt; k</code></pre></div><p>This automatically ensures that we don't use the <strong>same index twice</strong>.</p><hr><h1>8. Checking the Sum</h1><p>Inside the three loops:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span>(arr[i] + arr[j] + arr[k] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)</code></pre></div><p>Then:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">YES → valid triplet\nNO  → ignore it</code></pre></div><p>For example:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr = [-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>Suppose:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i → -1\nj → 0\nk → 1</code></pre></div><p>Then:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 0 + 1\n    ↓\n    0</code></pre></div><p>Therefore:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 0, 1]</code></pre></div><p>is a valid triplet.</p><hr><h1>9. Brute Force Dry Run</h1><p>Take:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr = [-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><h3><code>i = 0</code></h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i\n↓\n[-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]</code></pre></div><p>Now <code>j</code> starts from <code>i + 1</code>:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]\n     ↑\n     j</code></pre></div><p>Then <code>k</code> starts from:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">j + 1</code></pre></div><p>So:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]\n        ↑\n        k</code></pre></div><p>Check:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 0 + 1 = 0</code></pre></div><p>✅ Store:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 0, 1]</code></pre></div><p>Then <code>k</code> moves:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]\n           ↑\n           k</code></pre></div><p>Check:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 0 + 2 = 1</code></pre></div><p>❌ Not valid.</p><p>Then:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 0 + (-1) = -2</code></pre></div><p>❌</p><p>Then:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">-1 + 0 + (-4) = -5</code></pre></div><p>❌</p><p>Then <code>j</code> moves.</p><hr><h1>10. But Now Comes the Duplicate Problem</h1><p>Suppose our array contains:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>The loops might generate:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>But depending on the input/order, we could also generate the same values in another arrangement.</p><p>We need:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">UNIQUE TRIPLETS</code></pre></div><p>So we need some way of identifying:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>and:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>as the <strong>same triplet</strong>.</p><hr><h1>11. Solution for Duplicate Triplets</h1><p>The simple idea is:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Sort every triplet before storing it.</strong></p></blockquote><p>Suppose we generate:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, 2, -1]</code></pre></div><p>Sort it:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>Now suppose later we generate:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[2, -1, -1]</code></pre></div><p>Sort it:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>Both become exactly the same:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>Therefore, we can easily identify duplicates.</p><hr><h1>12. Visualization</h1><p>Before sorting:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Triplet 1:\n[-1, 2, -1]\n\nTriplet 2:\n[2, -1, -1]\n\nTriplet 3:\n[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>After sorting each:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Triplet 1 → [-1, -1, 2]\nTriplet 2 → [-1, -1, 2]\nTriplet 3 → [-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>Now all three are identical.</p><p>So we only need to store one.</p><hr><h1>13. Which Data Structure?</h1><p>We need a data structure that stores <strong>only unique values</strong>.</p><p>The obvious choice:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">SET</code></pre></div><p>A set automatically removes duplicates.</p><p>So our flow becomes:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Generate triplet\n       ↓\nSort triplet\n       ↓\nPut triplet into SET\n       ↓\nSET automatically keeps only unique triplets\n       ↓\nConvert SET → answer</code></pre></div><hr><h1>14. Brute Force Algorithm</h1><h3>Step 1</h3><p>Run three loops:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i\nj\nk</code></pre></div><p>such that:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i &lt; j &lt; k</code></pre></div><hr><h3>Step 2</h3><p>Check:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">arr[i] + arr[j] + arr[k] == 0</code></pre></div><hr><h3>Step 3</h3><p>If sum is <code>0</code>:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Create triplet</code></pre></div><hr><h3>Step 4</h3><p>Sort that triplet.</p><p>For example:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[2, -1, -1]\n       ↓\n[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><hr><h3>Step 5</h3><p>Insert it into a set.</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">SET\n ↓\n[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>If the same triplet comes again:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">[-1, -1, 2]</code></pre></div><p>the set will simply ignore it.</p><hr><h3>Step 6</h3><p>Finally:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">SET → answer</code></pre></div><p>and return the answer.</p><hr><h1>15. C++ Brute Force Code</h1><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">vector&lt;vector&lt;<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>&gt;&gt; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">threeSum</span>(vector&lt;<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>&gt;&amp; nums)\n{\n    set&lt;vector&lt;<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>&gt;&gt; st;\n\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> n = nums.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">size</span>();\n\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; n; i++)\n    {\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> j = i + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>; j &lt; n; j++)\n        {\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> k = j + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>; k &lt; n; k++)\n            {\n                <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span>(nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)\n                {\n                    vector&lt;<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>&gt; temp = {\n                        nums[i],\n                        nums[j],\n                        nums[k]\n                    };\n\n                    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sort</span>(temp.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">begin</span>(), temp.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">end</span>());\n\n                    st.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">insert</span>(temp);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    vector&lt;vector&lt;<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>&gt;&gt; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">ans</span>(\n        st.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">begin</span>(),\n        st.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">end</span>()\n    );\n\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> ans;\n}</code></pre></div><hr><h1>16. Code Flow Visualization</h1><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">                 ARRAY\n                   │\n                   ▼\n          ┌─────────────────┐\n          │    3 LOOPS      │\n          │  i → j → k      │\n          └────────┬────────┘\n                   │\n                   ▼\n        nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k]\n                   │\n             ┌─────┴─────┐\n             │           │\n            ≠ 0          = 0\n             │           │\n             │           ▼\n             │       Create triplet\n             │           │\n             │           ▼\n             │       Sort triplet\n             │           │\n             │           ▼\n             │        Insert SET\n             │           │\n             │           ▼\n             │     Unique automatically\n             │\n             ▼\n           Ignore</code></pre></div><hr><h1>17. Why <code>i + 1</code> and <code>j + 1</code>?</h1><p>This is an important interview point.</p><p>We could technically write:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">j = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>\nk = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span></code></pre></div><p>but then we would have to manually make sure:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i != j\nj != k\ni != k</code></pre></div><p>Instead, we naturally enforce:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i &lt; j &lt; k</code></pre></div><p>by doing:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> → n<span class=\"hljs-number\">-1</span>\n\nj = i + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> → n<span class=\"hljs-number\">-1</span>\n\nk = j + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> → n<span class=\"hljs-number\">-1</span></code></pre></div><p>Therefore:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">       i       j       k\n       ↓       ↓       ↓\n      [ ...  ...  ... ]</code></pre></div><p>The indices can never be equal.</p><hr><h1>18. Time Complexity</h1><p>We have <strong>three nested loops</strong>:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(i)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(j)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span>(k)</code></pre></div><p>Therefore:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(N³)</code></pre></div><p>The triplet is also sorted:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">cpp</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-cpp hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sort</span>(temp.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">begin</span>(), temp.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">end</span>());</code></pre></div><p>But there are only <strong>3 elements</strong> in the triplet.</p><p>Sorting 3 elements is effectively:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(1)</code></pre></div><p>So it doesn't change the major complexity.</p><hr><h2>SET Complexity</h2><p>We are inserting the triplet into a <code>set</code>.</p><p>Set insertion is approximately:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(log M)</code></pre></div><p>where <code>M</code> is the number of unique triplets currently stored.</p><p>Therefore, a more detailed complexity can be expressed as:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(N³ × log M)</code></pre></div><p>But the dominant part is:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(N³)</code></pre></div><hr><h1>19. Space Complexity</h1><p>We are using:</p><h3>① Set</h3><p>To store unique triplets:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(M)</code></pre></div><p>where <code>M</code> = number of unique triplets.</p><h3>② Answer</h3><p>We eventually store the triplets in:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">vector&lt;vector&lt;int&gt;&gt; ans</code></pre></div><p>So another:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(M)</code></pre></div><p>Therefore:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(M + M)</code></pre></div><p>or simply:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">O(M)</code></pre></div><p>where <code>M</code> is the number of unique triplets.</p><hr><h1>20. Interview Explanation</h1><p>If the interviewer asks:</p><blockquote><p><strong>\"Give me the brute-force solution.\"</strong></p></blockquote><p>You can say:</p><blockquote><p>\"Since I need to find all possible triplets, my first approach is to try every possible combination of three elements. I can use three nested loops where <code>i</code> represents the first element, <code>j</code> starts from <code>i+1</code>, and <code>k</code> starts from <code>j+1</code>, so that I never use the same index twice. Whenever <code>nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0</code>, I create that triplet. Since duplicate triplets are not allowed, I'll sort the three-element triplet and store it in a set. The set will automatically remove duplicate triplets.\"</p></blockquote><p>Then:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Time  → O(N³) approximately\nSpace → O(M), where M = unique triplets</code></pre></div><hr><h1>21. Brute Force — Mental Template</h1><p>Whenever you see:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Find all combinations of 3 elements satisfying some condition</strong></p></blockquote><p>immediately think:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">3 elements\n   ↓\n3 loops\n   ↓\ni, j, k\n   ↓\ncheck condition\n   ↓\nstore answer</code></pre></div><p>For this problem:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">3 elements\n   ↓\n3 loops\n   ↓\ni &lt; j &lt; k\n   ↓\nnums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0\n   ↓\nsort triplet\n   ↓\nset\n   ↓\nunique answer</code></pre></div><hr><h1>22. COMPLETE BRUTE FORCE FLOW</h1><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">                    3 SUM\n                      │\n                      ▼\n          Find 3 elements whose\n              sum = 0\n                      │\n                      ▼\n              Need UNIQUE\n               triplets\n                      │\n                      ▼\n              Try ALL triplets\n                      │\n                      ▼\n               3 Nested Loops\n                      │\n          ┌───────────┼───────────┐\n          ▼           ▼           ▼\n          i           j           k\n          │           │           │\n          │       i + 1       j + 1\n          │           │           │\n          └───────────┼───────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n       nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k]\n                      │\n                      ▼\n                   == 0 ?\n                 /       \\\n               NO         YES\n               │           │\n             Ignore        ▼\n                       Create triplet\n                           │\n                           ▼\n                       Sort triplet\n                           │\n                           ▼\n                        Insert SET\n                           │\n                           ▼\n                     Remove duplicates\n                           │\n                           ▼\n                     SET → ANSWER</code></pre></div><hr><h2>🔑 Brute Force Takeaways</h2><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">1. Need 3 elements\n       ↓\n   3 loops\n\n2. Avoid same index\n       ↓\n   i &lt; j &lt; k\n\n3. Check sum\n       ↓\n   nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0\n\n4. Duplicate triplets\n       ↓\n   Sort every triplet\n\n5. Store unique\n       ↓\n   Set\n\n6. Complexity\n       ↓\n   O(N³) approximately</code></pre></div><p><strong>Brute Force complete.</strong></p><p>When you say <strong><code>next</code></strong>, we'll move to the <strong>BETTER approach (O(N²) using hashing)</strong> in the <strong>same flow</strong>, with the same dry-run style and visualizations.</p>",
